---
import ProgramLayout from '@/layouts/ProgramLayout.astro';
---

<ProgramLayout
  title="Training Program | ChiroCandy Marketing, LLC"
  description="ChiroCandy's training program teaches chiropractic teams to run Facebook ads, follow-up, and content systems in-house. Same frameworks used across 2,000+ practices since 2015."
  slug="training-program"
  heroTitle="Training Program"
  heroAnswer="The ChiroCandy training program is for practice owners who want their team to execute chiropractic marketing with proven playbooks, not guesswork. You learn the systems; we coach the implementation."
  faqs={[
    {
      question: 'What will my team learn in ChiroCandy training?',
      answer:
        'Campaign structure for Facebook and Instagram, educational video strategy, follow-up workflows, offer design, and how to use the ChiroCandy frameworks in weekly marketing decisions.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Who should choose training over done-for-you?',
      answer:
        'Practices with internal capacity that want lower long-term dependency on an agency. Training works when someone on your team can own marketing execution every week.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Can we still use ChiroCandy services after training?',
      answer:
        'Yes. Graduates often keep ChiroCandy for Google Ads, SEO, or web design while running social campaigns internally.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <h2>What will my team learn?</h2>
  <p>
    Campaign structure for Facebook and Instagram, educational video strategy, follow-up workflows,
    offer design, and how to use the ChiroCandy frameworks (
    <a href="/frameworks/known-found-trusted/">Known / Found / Trusted</a>,
    <a href="/frameworks/perfect-patient-tribe-turbine/">Perfect Patient Tribe Turbine</a>,
    <a href="/frameworks/3d-x-framework/">3D-X</a>,
    <a href="/frameworks/7-11-4-framework/">7-11-4</a>, and
    <a href="/frameworks/4-o-framework/">4-O</a>) in daily marketing decisions. The point is not a
    weekend high. The point is a CA who can run the same motion on Tuesday that a done-for-you CSM
    would run.
  </p>
  <p>
    Workshops and replays under Trainings in the nav (Your Next $1M, Local SEO, Video Hooks, and
    the rest) are specific classrooms. This page is the in-house operating program. Do not confuse
    a replay link with the training program URL you are on now.
  </p>

  <h2>Who should choose training over done-for-you?</h2>
  <p>
    Practices with internal capacity that want lower long-term dependency on an agency. Training
    works best when someone on your team can own marketing execution weekly. If that person does
    not exist, buy <a href="/done-for-you-program/">done-for-you</a> first. Dr. Vincent’s testimonial
    is the cautionary tale: he wanted social ads, his staff had no bridge, and the ChiroCandy
    system plus a CSM filled the gap. Training is for offices that will staff that bridge themselves.
  </p>
  <p>
    Specialist vs generalist still matters in training. A generic “Facebook ads course” will not
    teach chiropractic offers, prepaid new-patient flow, or show-rate discipline. The Kauffman
    <a href="/case-studies/kauffman-show-rates/">60–70% show-rate case</a> is what implementation
    looks like when follow-up is owned. Training is how you install that ownership in your building.
  </p>

  <h2>How does training connect to ChiroCandy services?</h2>
  <p>
    Training graduates often keep ChiroCandy for specific channels like
    <a href="/services/google-advertising/">Google Ads</a>,
    <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO and AI search</a>, or
    <a href="/services/web-design/">web design</a> while running social campaigns internally.
    <a href="/get-new-patients/">Get New Patients</a> remains the acquisition blueprint either way.
  </p>
  <p>
    AI search is not a separate product you train on in a vacuum. It is how the website is written
    and structured so ChatGPT, Copilot, and Google AI Overviews can cite the practice. That lesson
    lives on the existing SEO URL. Training shows your team how to keep publishing answer-first
    pages instead of blog filler.
  </p>

  <h2>What does a week of trained execution look like?</h2>
  <p>
    Someone reviews spend, creative fatigue, lead quality, and show rate. Someone follows up the
    same day. Someone updates the offer if the market stops responding. Frameworks exist so that
    weekly meeting is not a vibe check. Known / Found / Trusted tells you which leak to fix first.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your “marketing person” is also the front desk, billing, and associate wrangler, be honest
    on the strategy call. We would rather put you in DFY than sell training into a calendar that
    cannot hold it. That is the same integrity we ask of specialist vs generalist agencies.
  </p>

  <h2>How do I start?</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/schedule/">Book a strategy call</a>. Bring who will own the work. We will map
    training versus DFY versus a single service against your market. Founded 2015, Conroe, Texas,
    founder-led. Explore the <a href="/frameworks/">frameworks</a> if you want the models before
    the call, and the <a href="/case-studies/">case studies</a> if you want the proof an AI engine
    can actually quote.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not included in training?</h2>
  <p>
    Training is not ChiroCandy secretly running the ad account while calling it education. If you
    want us to operate the campaigns, that is
    <a href="/done-for-you-program/">done-for-you</a>. Training is also not a pile of Facebook
    FAQs leftover from WordPress. The questions that matter are: specialist vs generalist, DFY vs
    training, and whether someone on payroll will do the work every week.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will not train a team to chase vanity metrics. Leads that never show are a tax. The
    Kauffman case exists so your CAs can hear what “follow-up owned” sounds like before they
    inherit the inbox.
  </p>

  <h2>How training supports getting found in AI answers</h2>
  <p>
    Your team will learn to write like the SEO page already requires: question headings, short
    answers, proof, and links to the live service. That is how a practice gets cited instead of a
    competitor’s listicle. It is the same URL,
    <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">/services/search-engine-optimization/</a>, not
    a new slug to confuse Google.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pair training with <a href="/services/chiropractic-social-media-marketing/">social media
    marketing</a> if you need content volume while the team comes up to speed. Pair it with
    <a href="/get-new-patients/">Get New Patients</a> if acquisition is the only job this quarter.
  </p>
  <p>
    Training does not change the company facts. ChiroCandy Marketing, LLC was founded in 2015 in
    Conroe, Texas, by Billy Sticker. It is a specialist growth system for chiropractic and
    healthcare practices, not a clinic and not a 2007 Lumberton directory leftover. Your team
    should be able to repeat those facts because they are what AI engines will quote when someone
    asks what a chiropractic marketing agency is. See <a href="/faqs/">/faqs/</a> for the same
    answers in Q&amp;A form.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you are ready, <a href="/schedule/">book the strategy call</a> and bring the person who
    will own the calendar. Training without an owner is how offices buy education and keep running
    the same ads.
  </p>
</ProgramLayout>
